  "notes": "All 3 files processed for KPCL (single facility, IDCOL loan, USD, LIBOR/Term-SOFR + margin floating rate mechanism throughout — never a pure RATE_CHANGE event because the loan's rate BASIS never changed at a restructure boundary in isolation; rate resets are inherent to the floating-rate mechanism every quarter, so rateBeforePercent/rateAfterPercent are set to null for all 3 versions since none of the events was itself a discrete rate-basis change).\n\nCross-checks performed: (1) V1's opening balance (47,000,000) exactly equals the original 60-installment schedule's closing balance as of 2021-03-15 (period 6). (2) V2's opening balance (42,648,148.15) exactly equals V1's closing balance as of 2022-06-15 (period 11). (3) V3's opening balance (40,907,407.41) exactly equals V2's closing balance as of 2023-06-15. In all three cases principal_schedule_amounts sum exactly to the version's opening balance and finalClosingBalance is ~0 (full amortization within that version's own horizon), confirming clean event boundaries with zero capitalization, zero waiver, and zero overdue roll-in at any of the three events.\n\nEvent-by-event interpretation:\n1. \"1st Restructured (Jun'21)\" — effective 2021-06-15 (period 7 of the original 60). The original schedule had a stepped principal-percentage profile (1.0% -> 1.8% -> 2.0% -> 3.0% -> 1.4% of original principal per quarter). This restructure flattens all 54 remaining installments into a single level principal amount of 870,370.37/quarter (= 47,000,000 / 54), leaving total tenor (60 installments, maturity 18-Oct-2034) and the LIBOR+4.50% floating-rate mechanism unchanged. Classified RESTRUCTURE (principal profile changed, not merely the rate).\n\n2. \"2nd Restructured (Dec'22)\" — effective 2022-09-15. Two consecutive principal payments (2022-09-15 and 2022-12-15) are deferred to Rs./USD 0 (a 2-quarter/6-month principal moratorium; interest continues to accrue and is paid current each period, so nothing capitalizes), and the tenor is extended by exactly 2 installments (60 -> 62 total, maturity pushed from 18-Oct-2034 to 15-Mar-2035) to fully recover the deferred principal via the same 870,370.37 level installment for all remaining periods. Workbook annotates this row explicitly as \"Principal deferred\" / \"Tenor extension\". Classified RESTRUCTURE. tenorMonthsBefore/After computed as 60x3=180 and 62x3=186 quarterly months (approximate, based on installment count x 3-month frequency).\n\n3. \"Prepayment Sep'23\" — per the task's specific modeling instruction, this is NOT a full reschedule. The workbook shows: normal amortization through 2023-06-15 under the 2nd-restructured schedule; then a payment-received breakdown table showing a remittance of 5,966,035 on/around 2023-09-10/11/13 covering Principal Overdue (966,035) + LPC Overdue (0, separately tracked/adjusted) + a genuine Prepayment tranche of 5,000,000 (dated 13-Sep-23); a second prepayment tranche of 1,897,867 landed on 17-Dec-23. Total prepayment across both tranches = 6,897,867 (this is the borrower-specific field the schema has no dedicated slot for — captured here in notes per instructions). I modeled this as: (a) an ad-hoc row on 2023-09-13 with interest=0, principal=5,000,000, closing balance stepped down accordingly (opening 40,907,407.41 -> closing 35,907,407.41); (b) the already-scheduled regular installment on 2023-09-17 (870,370.37, unchanged); (c) the second prepayment tranche folded into the 2023-12-17 installment, which jumps to 2,768,237.00 (= the regular 870,370.37 + the 1,897,867 tranche, netted against a small rounding/LPC adjustment per the workbook's own figures — used the workbook's actual value verbatim via override rather than re-deriving it); (d) from 2024-03-18 onward (the first full quarter after both prepayments are absorbed), the remaining 48 installments are RECOMPUTED to a new smaller level amount of 717,084.4452674898/quarter (= new balance 32,268,800.04 / 45 remaining periods after 2024-03-18, consistent with the re-leveling behavior IDCOL uses per prior research), with the original 62-installment/15-Mar-2035 tenor preserved (not shortened) as confirmed by the workbook annotation \"sanction advice dated 13 Mar 24: tenor has been reinstated to 15 Mar 35\" (a benchmark/tenor note also mentioning a transient tenor reduction to 15-Jun-33 that was later reversed — final state uses 15-Mar-2035, which is what this version's params reflect). Classified PREPAYMENT with effectiveDate = 2023-09-13 (the date of the first ad-hoc paydown), num_installments=48 counted from that date through loan maturity. Benchmark also transitioned from 3M USD LIBOR to 3M USD Term SOFR + CAS 0.26% within this same file's window (per an explicit workbook annotation), which is a separate benchmark-transition/regulatory event bundled into the same file rather than a discrete restructure of its own — noted here for completeness but not broken out as its own version entry since it is not accompanied by a distinct balance/tenor discontinuity and the file provides only one unified post-prepayment schedule.\n\nAll params objects use principal_type=\"Scheduled Principal\" with full override arrays (opening_balance_amounts / interest_payment_amounts / closing_balance_amounts / principal_schedule_amounts) pinned row-by-row to the workbook's actual figures, mirroring the SCBL/MCML/QPSL/SKS/THERMAX override pattern already used in examples.ts EX_DATA, since these historical restructure schedules include irregular stub periods, moratorium zeros, and manually-adjusted prepayment-absorption rows that cannot be cleanly re-derived from a single first-principles formula. interest_rate (top-level, decimal fraction) in each version's params is set to that version's first-period rate (for engine-default consistency), but the authoritative per-period rates are the interest_rates_by_period array. All three versions' repayment_dates / rates / principal / opening / interest / closing arrays were extracted directly from each workbook's \"KPCL_Loan\" sheet (the active/authoritative schedule tab in each file — the \"Repayment Schedule\" tab in the Jun'21 file was found to still contain the untouched ORIGINAL 60-installment schedule for reference/comparison and was not used as a source). No DFIM circular or explicit Bangladesh Bank approval reference was found in any of the 3 workbooks for the two restructures; only the prepayment file references a specific \"sanction advice dated 13 Mar 24\" tied to the tenor reinstatement."
